                      %mo −
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\text{It is convenient and meaningful to declare the notational conventions to:}
                  \\phantom{--------------------}
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                abbreviate
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi.mathscript ℋ
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ≔
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mo !
                      %msub
                        %mi.mathscript ℋ
                        %mo •
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ≃
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mi.mathscript ℋ
                        %mo •
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{H} \,\coloneqq\, p_! \mathscr{H}_\bullet \,\simeq\, p_\ast \mathscr{H}_\bullet
            %li
              %p
                notationally suppress any outer application of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mi B
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi LinType
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi LinType
                          %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p_B)^\ast \colon LinType \to LinType_B
          %p
            Thereby, the definiteness/randomness modalities in relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/necessity+and+possibility"} necessity and possibility
            of classical modal logic (
            %a{:href => "#ClassicalModalLogic"}> above
            ) may be expressed in quantum modal logic by:
          %div{:style => "margin: -10px 0px 20px 10px"}
            %img{:src => "/nlab/files/DefinitelyRandomlyViaPossiblyNecessarily.jpg", :width => "180px"}/
          %p
            This way, the default
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            for modal quantum logic is that of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundles"} bundles
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+dimensional+vector+spaces"} finite dimensional vector spaces
            (finite-dimensional complex
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+spaces"} Hilbert spaces
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+sets"} finite sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mi C
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo !
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p_C)_!
            as well as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mi C
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p_C)_\ast
            yield the ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibers"} fibers
            (a
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/biproduct"} biproduct
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            under which the following type theory describes the traditional
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+circuits"} quantum circuits
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+linear+type"} dependent linear type
            by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mo •
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi LinType
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{H}_\bullet : LinType_C
            and its generic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/term"} term
            by the usual notation for
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+states"} quantum states
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %msub
                    %mi ψ
                    %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mi c
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  c : C
                  \\;\;\;
                  \\vdash
                  \\;\;\;
                  \\vert \psi_c \rangle \;\colon\; \mathcal{H}_c
                  \\,.
          %p
            one finds for the base change
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+linear+types"} dependent linear types
            along
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/family+of+finite+types"} finite fibers
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:FiniteBaseType"} (?)
            that the interpretation of their (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/counit+of+a+comonad"}> co-
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+a+monad"} units
            is as follows:
          %p
            By the assumption that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite
            and since
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"} Vect
            has
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/biproducts"} biproducts
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
          .maruku-equation
