          %p This way, one finds that the four (co)unit operations of quantum modal logic are given as follows:
          #eq:QuantumModalUnits.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
            %code.maruku-mathml
          %div{:style => "margin: -10px 0px 20px 10px"}
            %img{:src => "/nlab/files/QCwthLHT-QuantumModalUnits-230806.jpg", :width => "840px"}/
          %h3#TheQuantumModality Quantum modality
          %p
            In addition to the above
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+scheme"} schemata
            of (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonad"}> co
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monads"} monads
            acting on the (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+linear+type"}> dependent
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+type"} linear
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+systems"} type systems
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+monad"} relative monad
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Q
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mtd
                          %mi Type
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mi LType
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↦
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨁
                            %mi B
                          %mi 𝟙
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\mathrm{Q}
                  \&amp;\colon&amp;
                  Type &amp;\longrightarrow&amp;
                  LType
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp;
                  B &amp;\mapsto&amp; \underset{B}{\bigoplus} \mathbb{1}
                  }
          %p
            which sends a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+type"} finite type
            (in particular) to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
            that it
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+span"} spans
            (a detailed description of this relative monad is
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "relative+monad#LinearSpan"} here
          %p
            This is in fact
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+monad"} idempotent
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            on the full
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+linear+type"} dependent linear
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+system"} type system
            that this relative monad is induced by is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+monad"} idempotent monad
            which witnesses a
            = succeed "-inclusion" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategory
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Q
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Type
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %mi 𝟙
                  %mi DLType
                  %mo ↠
                  %mi LType
                  %mover
                    %mo ↪
                    %mphantom
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo −
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi DLType
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
